alright in pokemon brilliant diamond and  shining pearl once you beat cynthia and  are crowned the champion of the sinnoh  region you might be thinking well now  what here are seven things that you  should do in detail once you hit the  post game drop a like hit that sub and  keep your comments about experience all  to yourself let's get to it  so the most important thing that you  should aim to do in my opinion once you  hit the credits is to unlock your  national decks it's not as difficult as  it might seem at first although if  you've been skipping a lot of trainer  battles during the main game then you  might have some backtracking to do to  unlock the national decks you don't need  to catch them all you only need to see  every pokemon in the sino deck  specifically usually folks might be  missing an unknown and they can find it  in the unknown cave east of selassian  town or they have not seen the legendary  exclusive from the other version however  if you go to celestic town and speak to  cynthia's grandmother she'll show you  the legendary from the other version so  the legendary in question would be  palkia and brilliant diamond or dialga  in shining pearl when you have seen all  150 pokemon of the sinnoh decks go to  san gemtown and speak to professor rowan  a quick cutscene will show where  professor oak appears and he mentions  how he was passing by and he meant to  share his national dex upgrades and  since you're there he'll give you a free  upgrade as well when you unlock the  national decks the rest of the post game  will fall into place a lot easier you  will start encountering many pokemon  that did not appear throughout the core  game especially in the grand underground  having the national decks will also make  sure that for each new pokemon you see  or catch you will have the most  up-to-date entries possible  so for pokemon veterans i know that the  core game must have felt easy if you  would like somewhat of a more demanding  challenge go ahead and take advantage of  replaying against trainers and leaders  that are itching for a second crack at  you be warned though their teams have  significant upgrades now and every gym  leader's pokemon level is well into the  high 60s and 70s not sure how often you  can farm the gym leaders though i  believe it is just the one rematch with  each leader however you can definitely  keep battling the elite for as long as  you'd like lastly you can use the versus  seeker a key item that lets you see  which trainers in sinnoh want to battle  you you'll notice a little double  exclamation point appear over their head  if the versus seeker spots them and  manually speak to them to trigger the  fight their pokemon usually aren't that  strong but it's a good way to pass the  time  so for those of you into competitive  battling you can tackle the battle tower  once you beat the main game go to  snowpoint city and talk to the sailor  just before entering the city and he  will take you to what is known as the  fight area this port town leads to the  battle tower stark mountain and other  endgame areas like the survival and  resort areas as the name suggests the  battle tower is for  well battling you can do single battles  or double battles and you fight seven  trainers in a row with the final trainer  in each block being a kind of a mini  boss if you successfully get a streak of  49 wins or more you can unlock the  master variant of single and double  battles the battle tower is basically a  good place to farm bps or battle points  to exchange them for tms or items that  can be used to mess with your pokemon  stats this helps their development to  max the stats that they favor and it  avoids investing ev or effort value  points into the stats that they won't  rely on to help with better  understanding your pokemon's potential  you can unlock the judge function in the  battle tower simply walk to the dude in  the battle tower center near the right  side of the room and speak to him that's  all it takes and he'll unlock the  function for you now when you inspect  your pokemon you can press the plus or  minus buttons and you'll see your  pokemon's ivs or intrinsic values there  is a  whole process of breeding using dittos  and destiny knots to get eggs that will  hatch with high level ivs combined with  the nature that you want or using bottle  caps for hyper training a lot of that  gets real nitty gritty and it's honestly  worth its own video breakdown sometime  later  so the first time you arrive at the new  battle area you'll run into some  punk-ass kid named buck who basically  challenges you to try to beat him  getting to stark mountain fast forward  and the whole point of stark mountain is  for you to unlock one of the legendaries  there's a brief quest with buck inside  stark mountain where you will want to  keep your eyes peeled for a magma stone  which buck will snag after he teams up  with you yeah i'm not happy about it  either find him later at his home though  and talk to him and he will revisit the  area in stark mountain saying that he is  going to return the magma stone when you  return to stark mountain after you speak  to buck you will see heatran appear  catch it and add it to your collection  of legendaries that brilliant diamond  and shining pearl have to offer and  we'll go into more detail on the other  legendaries later in this video  when exploring the cinno region many of  these activities can technically be done  during the main game although some  trainers might have forgotten about them  because their goal is usually to get to  the lead for asap or at least that's how  i usually play still a few of these are  contingent on you becoming champion  first so now that you can focus more on  the open world it is a good time to  revisit and explore sinnoh in greater  detail one thing that i'd like to do is  farm berries there is an excellent plot  of soil next to most major cities some  even a few steps away from the pokemon  centers this makes it easy to multiply  hard to find berries used for puffin  making using poffins will help your  pokemon perform better in super contests  which can be a nice change of pace from  the typical pokedex and battle questing  sign up your pokemon for the super  contest in hartham city and shine  brighter than the competition with the  chance to get plenty of ribbons a  pokemon with 10 ribbons will grant you  access to this prestigious looking  building in the resort area because if  you don't have enough ribbons you'll  simply be met with a very snooty looking  npc at the door that will kick you out  you can also retrace your steps and find  items that were previously out of reach  by using all of the hms you've unlocked  by beating the agent leaders or by  talking to people go west of sunny shore  to that one rich resort area known as  the valor lakefront with the blue  rooftops and speak to a man that will  grant you an oval charm although the  catches you have to battle him first and  the person is none other than game  freak's morimoto his team is kind of a  pain of the ass too at least the jolteon  was for me the game directors also have  characters representing themselves in  that area you can talk to both to  receive a sinodex certificate once you  have the national decks and a catching  charm there is also a long-haired  musician in the room and talking to him  reveals that he is actually the game's  sound designer and he's going to gift  you after your champion the ogds sounds  this is a fun perk letting you listen to  the original music as they were in gen  4's diamond and pearl on nintendo ds  then there's baby the creator of the  pokemon storage system in this gen and  visiting her in hartham city will result  in receiving a level 5 evie from her in  the post game after you are champion  there are more legendary pokemon to hunt  some of them like cresselia and giratina  can be caught in game by talking to  people to trigger the quest or simply  finding their locations like the turn  back cave there was also rotom which you  can battle and catch by going to eternal  forest talk to gardenia and enter the  haunted mansion in eternity forest rotum  is at a super low level which means that  catching it should be no problem you  will receive a secret key after you have  caught rotom and that secret key will  let you evolve rotom into different  forms at a secret lab in galactic tower  simply go to that galactic building in  eterna city use the seeker key on the  first floor to let you enter a room with  all of the other appliances throwing  rotom into the appliances will unlock  the rotom catalog allowing you to change  rotom's form and even its moves  if you're interested in legendary  pokemon from other generations you'll  need to spend time in romana's park once  you arrive at the park by traveling  south of san jam and to the east oak  will give you a chain counter app on the  poke speak to the vendors in the park to  trade in mysterious shards for unique  slates that will let you catch  legendaries within the caves at romana's  park note that the legendaries have a  particular order it starts with the  three regis allowing you to battle  reggie gigas in snow point once the  three reggies are all caught brilliant  diamond owners will have the three  legendary beasts up next and ho-oh while  shining pearl will get the three  legendary birds and lugia there's also  even a level 100 giratina at the very  end that you can only battle you cannot  catch this pokemon and the reason is  your whole goal is to obtain its held  item the held item is an orb that will  allow you to transform your own giratina  into its special platinum origin form  the trick is acquiring the slates which  you can only get by trading in  mysterious shards which come in small  and large forms to get enough mysterious  shards you're gonna have to spend a lot  of time digging in the underground  you first gain access to the underground  mid game thanks to the underground man  in eterna city next to the pokemon  center and the quest that he will give  to you still the grand underground area  becomes way more relevant in the post  game especially with the national decks  i have spent an unholy amount of time in  this area armed to the teeth with quick  balls dust balls netballs all of it and  just going to town on everything there's  so many kanto jodo and hoen pokemon to  catch even including all the starters so  if you want a typhlosion in the game  take your time in the underground i  mentioned earlier that you need  mysterious shards and this is where you  farm them press r on your switch to send  out a scanning pulse whenever you see  shining dots on your map letting you  know that there is a treasure nearby to  dig up interact with the glittering dots  on the walls when you see them and a  treasure digging mini-game will come up  you use two different tools one light  and one heavy to chip away at the wall  but be careful though because you can't  just go ham otherwise the wall could  collapse as indicated by the cracks  appearing at the top of the screen in  general though the treasure is worth  farming because you can get rare  evolution stones or even boxes with  pokemon statues in them use the statues  that you get from the boxes to fill out  your secret base which can easily be  made by using a digger tool acquired  from the underground man or from some  vendors in the grand underground area  the type of statues that you display  will affect the spawn rates of certain  pokemon types in the underground as well  digletts and doug trios around the  underground will leave something  glittering on the ground you'll want to  walk over it to fill up a progress bar  that is listed out of 40. each diglett  counts as one and a dub trio counts as  three if you get the progress bar  complete to 40 out of 40 you will hear  an alarm as well as an alert that says  something good will happen what occurs  is that when you dig up items the odds  of you receiving a rare gorgeous box  from the treasure dramatically increases  you are also more likely to see shiny  pokemon appear in the grand underground  and this effect will last for about  three to five minutes from what i could  see before the progress bar resets back  to zero i strongly recommend that you  connect to the internet when you go to  the underground you don't really  interact too much with other players  anyway but the progress bar will factor  in everyone's progress in the  underground so it is by far the fastest  way to max that bar out so you can make  the most out of the buffs  there are some more post game stuff but  they're not available to players just  yet still it seems like those events  will become available in future updates  to brilliant diamond and shining pearl  so if you've enjoyed your time with the  game tell me all about in the comments i  would love to hear about your experience  what teams you're rocking in the battle  tower and what your favorite legendary  is until next time  [Music]  you

